Midgaard's Three Civic Oaths anchor warden legitimacy doctrine and road administration ritual.
Oath of Light: no ward unlit, no traveler uncounted.
Oath of Stone: no judgment hidden, no sentence unrecorded.
Oath of Bread: no levy taken that cannot be borne.
These oaths shaped checkpoint practice, boundary-sigil maintenance, and the legal theater of visible jurisdiction.
